
# Project: Autopilot — MOEX order-book scalping

## General workflow
- Work with the existing codebase; do not recreate the project.
- Inspect the architecture, dependencies, configuration, and tests before changing code.
- Implement requested changes directly in the existing project directory.
- Preserve existing behavior and public interfaces unless explicitly asked to change them.
- Make small, focused changes instead of unnecessary rewrites.
- Explain which files changed and why.
- Run relevant tests and report their actual results.
- Never claim a test passed unless it was executed successfully.

## Trading safety
- Never submit real exchange orders or enable live trading autonomously.
- Never connect to a live brokerage account or use real trading credentials.
- Never expose API keys, tokens, passwords, or account identifiers.
- Do not change live-trading, risk-limit, or order-execution behavior without explicit approval.
- Prefer mocked exchange interfaces, historical data, and paper trading for tests.
- Never remove risk controls to make a test pass.
- Preserve order-book sequencing, timestamps, and price/quantity precision.
- Explicitly handle stale market data, disconnects, and rejected orders.

## File and command safety
- Work only inside the selected project directory unless authorized otherwise.
- Ask before deleting files, changing dependencies, running migrations, or modifying infrastructure.
- Ask before running any command that can connect to a live exchange or execute trades.
- Do not overwrite unrelated user changes.
- Never commit or push changes without permission.

## Before finishing
- Summarize changed files and behavior.
- Report tests run, failures, and unresolved risks.
- Identify any changes that still require manual verification.
